xnu 0177: bring the GMU up: SMMU context, firmware and HFI

The CX domain, hub and GMU clocks were up but every GMU register read
0xdeafbead and the GX GDSC stayed off. Two bugs: the gen7 register numbers
are dword offsets (byte offset = word*4 - 0x68000), and the GMU needs both
SMMU streams (SID 5 and 0x405). With the corrected offsets, the GBIF halt
cleared, the GMU context bank programmed (CBAR/CBA2R/TCR/TCR2/MAIR/TTBR0),
the TCM blocks and the 57 KiB external code block loaded at IOVA 0x4000,
and the HFI queue table published, the CM3 reaches FW_INIT_RESULT=0x100 in
about 1.8 ms and HFI_CTRL_STATUS=0x1. CORE_FW_START (HFI id 14) is
accepted. The RSCC/PDC setup and the HFI PERF/BW power tables are not sent
yet, so GX stays off. gmustart=1 gates the new path. The firmware header
(mondrian_gmu_fw.h) is generated by tools/gen-gmu-fw.py from the device
dump and is not committed; a build without it keeps the old behaviour.
